turen-binary-diff-wasm
Copyright (c) 2026 Turen Labs

This package contains Turen's bounded WebAssembly binary differencing and
patching module. The diff scan in src/bsdiff.rs is an original
single-threaded Rust port of the bsdiff-style partition scan from
divvun/bidiff 1.0.0 (Apache-2.0 OR MIT,
https://github.com/divvun/bidiff), itself derived from Colin Percival's
bsdiff (BSD-2-Clause); the rayon and wall-clock paths upstream uses are not
present here. Patches use the upstream bipatch wire format and are applied
by the unmodified bipatch crate.

Built from the following permissively licensed crates.io dependencies:

- bipatch 1.0.0 (Apache-2.0 OR MIT) — bipatch patch stream decoder
  (https://github.com/divvun/bidiff)
- divsufsort 2.0.0 + sacabase 2.0.0 (MIT) — suffix array construction and
  longest-substring-match search
  (https://github.com/fasterthanlime/stringsearch)
- byteorder 1.5.0 (Unlicense OR MIT) — little-endian header fields
- integer-encoding 2.1.3 (MIT) — varint control records
- data-encoding 2.11.1 (MIT) — canonical base64 for the JSON input document
- sha2 0.11.0 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) — RustCrypto SHA-256 for reported digests
  and expectedSha256 output verification
- serde 1.0.228 / serde_json 1.0.145 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) — report model and
  JSON envelopes
- wasm-bindgen 0.2.108 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) — JavaScript bindings

The full dependency closure is recorded in Cargo.lock; every entry is
permissively licensed. No GPL, LGPL, or proprietary code is linked into the
module. All operations are deterministic, offline byte processing over
caller-supplied buffers: no filesystem, network, subprocess, environment,
or clock access.
